notes.body:
@martin.r.mathieson just for the record...

Regarding `tfs_downlink_uplink = { "Downlink", "Uplink" };`, I checked other protocols/dissectors and it seems instead of `tfs_downlink_uplink` many of them use `value_string direction_vals[]` concept.

Logically the same but sometimes simply using bool would be better, I guess?

For example:

`packet-log3gpp.c`
```c

static const value_string direction_vals[] = {
    { 0,   "Uplink" },
    { 1,   "Downlink" },
    { 0,   NULL },
};
...
        { &hf_log3gpp_direction,
            { "Direction",
              "log3gpp.direction", FT_UINT8, BASE_DEC, VALS(direction_vals), 0x0,
              "Frame direction (Uplink or Downlink)", HFILL
            }
        },
```

`packet-umts_rlc.c`
```
/* Link direction */
#define LINK_DIR_UNKNOWN    -1
#define P2P_DIR_UL  0
#define P2P_DIR_DL  1
...
static const value_string rlc_dir_vals[] = {
    { P2P_DIR_UL, "Uplink" },
    { P2P_DIR_DL, "Downlink" },
    { 0, NULL }
};
...
        { &hf_rlc_channel_dir,
          { "Direction", "rlc.channel.dir",
            FT_UINT8, BASE_DEC, VALS(rlc_dir_vals), 0, NULL, HFILL }
```

`packet-rlc-lte.c`
```
/* direction */
#define DIRECTION_UPLINK 0
#define DIRECTION_DOWNLINK 1
...
static const value_string direction_vals[] =
{
    { DIRECTION_UPLINK,      "Uplink"},
    { DIRECTION_DOWNLINK,    "Downlink"},
    { 0, NULL }
};
...
        { &hf_rlc_lte_context_direction,
            { "Direction",
              "rlc-lte.direction", FT_UINT8, BASE_DEC, VALS(direction_vals), 0x0,
              "Direction of message", HFILL
            }
        },
```

